[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...d5 4.fxe5 Nxe4 5.Nf3 Bc5"]
[Start "vienna-gambit 5.Nf3"]

5... Bc5 { Black's most accurate fifth move: the bishop eyes f2 and the knight on e4 is protected by the pawn on d5. } 6. d4 { Hits the bishop and takes the centre. The pawn on d4 also keeps the bishop away from f2. } 6... Bb4 ( 6... Bb6 7. Bb5+ { Check, and White castles next while the bishop sits out of play on b6. } 7... Nc6 8. O-O ) 7. Bd2 { Defends the knight on c3 and breaks the pin, so ...Nxc3 would not win anything. } 7... Nxd2 { Black trades knight for bishop. } 8. Qxd2 { Recaptures with the queen so the pawn structure stays healthy, and the queen eyes the bishop on b4. } 8... O-O 9. a3 { Asks the bishop on b4 a question: take on c3 or go back. Either way White keeps the centre. } 9... Be7 10. Bd3 { Develops towards the king side and prepares to castle. Plan: castle, then play Ng5 or Qe3 against the king; the extra centre pawns give White the freer game. } *
